  "title": "Linear flows: vertex-root pair failures are #P-hard when the dual slot has no degree-1 data",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "When a class-3 edge fails only the vertex-root condition and its dual slot carries no degree-1 data, the conserved vertex flow and the dual slot's constraints are linear in that slot's data, so every Fourier-dual weight counts solutions of linear equations and is non-negative. With the Brunnian rank witness this gives #P-hardness, deciding 8 more census algebras and, with conserved flows, the whole vertex-root family.",
